 "reading": "NAS100 2016 → now −0.004R net (n 2040, month t −0.16, Holm p 1; gross +0.055R, gross t +2.58; 2016-20 −0.035R, 2021 → now +0.023R; at 2x costs −0.062R; 34 of 40 placebos beaten; failed: isPos, t2, holm, cost2x, placebo). SPX500 2016 → now −0.036R net (n 2015, month t −1.64, Holm p 1; gross +0.032R, gross t +1.49; 2016-20 −0.039R, 2021 → now −0.033R; at 2x costs −0.103R; 25 of 40 placebos beaten; failed: isPos, oosPos, t2, holm, cost2x, placebo). Pooled (descriptive, not a test): −0.020R net (n 4055, month t −0.99; gross +0.043R, t +2.30). Costs take 0.059R a trade on NAS100 and 0.067R on SPX500 (2016-20 0.097R / 0.098R, when the index levels were lower and a fixed point cost was a larger share of 1R; gold's out-of-sample cost was about 0.05R). Before costs the breakout is positive on NAS100 (gross month t +2.58) and positive on SPX500 (gross t +1.49), smaller than on gold (+0.121R a trade gross 2021 → now); as on silver, gross and net split: the lean survives on paper before costs and not after. Neither market passes: the same rule does not carry from gold to the US index CFDs, so on this evidence the gold result (with its 2007-15 replication) is a gold-specific effect, not a general intraday volatility-breakout effect. Not an edge on indices; nothing live changes and no proposal is written."
}
